# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# SDR captures: ELRS Find sweeps save to captures/elrs_find_*/. The WHOLE capture
# folder is SYNCED via git — raw IQ (.complex8/.cf32/.iq) AND the per-channel
# metadata (.meta.txt/.json/manifest.json) — so the other session gets every
# channel's samples to deep-analyze. The pre-push hook (scripts/git/pre-push)
# auto-commits captures/ on every `git push`, so new sweeps upload with no manual
# `git add`. Everything that looks like a stray capture OUTSIDE captures/ stays
# ignored (the blanket *.complex8 etc. below), and the `!captures/**` lines
# re-include the capture subtree.
#   NOTE: a full 80-ch sweep is ~160 MB, and git keeps every version forever, so
#   this grows .git over time. To reclaim it later: delete dead captures (they
#   leave history) then do a coordinated `git filter-repo` + re-clone.
#
#   WIDEBAND single-file grabs (.cdif BLUE files) are GB-scale (the 28 MS/s
#   2450 MHz grabs are 740 MB and 3.25 GB). Per operator decision (2026-10-08):
#   .cdif under captures/ IS synced via git like the rest of the raw IQ — same
#   "push everything" policy already chosen for .complex8/.cf32. Accepted
#   tradeoff: GB-scale pushes, kept in git history forever (reclaiming it later
#   needs a coordinated `git filter-repo` + force-push + everyone re-clones —
#   not done casually). .sigmf-data/.cfile are a DIFFERENT, not-yet-decided
#   case and stay ignored everywhere until asked about. A stray *.cdif OUTSIDE
#   captures/ also stays ignored (only the capture tree re-includes it).
*.iq
*.complex8
*.cf32
*.jsonl
*.cdif
*.sigmf-data
*.cfile
# Captures are UNTRACKED (2026-10-10, operator request): the 503 tracked capture
# files (8.9 GB) were git-rm --cached so they stop weighing down every push.
# They stay on disk (the laptop has them); the pushed copies stay in history
# (no rewrite, per the no-force-push rule). To keep them out of git going
# forward, the whole captures/ tree is ignored — the pre-push hook's
# `git add -- captures/` finds nothing to add. If a specific capture needs to be
# shared, `git add -f captures/<file>` overrides the ignore for that one file.
captures/

# C++ build artifacts (cpp/build.sh produces these)
cpp/elrs_intercept
cpp/tests/test_elrs_decode
cpp/tests/test_lora_demod
cpp/test_elrs_decode
cpp/test_lora_demod
cpp/*.bin
cpp/*.o

